  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Countywide Sanitation Activity (CWSA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Liberia):  USAID has finalized the selection.of an apparently successful applicant for the new Countywide Sanitation.Activity to complement existing health and behavior change activities. The new.mechanism will specifically target the 60 percent of Liberians living in five.counties who have limited access to basic sanitation services. .Using FY 2022 WASH funds, USAID will implement the Countywide Sanitation.Activity that will focus on eliminating open defecation in five counties.(Montserrado, Nimba, Lofa, Bong, and Grand Bassa).  These counties.represent more than 60 percent of all the people in Liberia currently.practicing open defecation. The new activity will 1) improve sanitation.governance at both the national and county levels, improve sector coordination,.monitoring, reporting, and evidence-based planning and budgeting for.sanitation; 2) ensure the adoption of key sanitation behaviors, including.eliminating open defecation and supporting sustainable construction of latrines.and toilets; 3) strengthen sanitation markets through the development and.sharing of information about opportunities and services, and capacity-building.of small businesses involved in sanitation, and 4) increase financing for.sanitation at the national, county, and household levels, through improved.resource mobilization and tracking. The goal of the activity is to sustainably.move everyone currently practicing open defecation in the five counties to a.basic level of sanitation. Of the total funding allocated to this activity,.$1,000,000 will meet the Safe Latrines non-SPSD earmark. In addition, all FY.2022 funding allocated to this IM contributes to meeting the required water.earmark. Engineering analysis preceding design activities will include consideration of climate change and its potential impacts on the location (siting), functionality and sustainability of resulting sanitation facilities..</narrative>
  </description>
